  },
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> be a relation on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>Z</mi></math> defined by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>d</mi><mo>)</mo></math> if and only if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi></math> is divisible by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> . Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Reflexive and symmetric but not transitive",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Reflexive but neither symmetric not transitive",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Reflexive, symmetric and transitive",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Reflexive and transitive but not symmetric",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given relation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo> </mo><mo>:</mo><mo> </mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi>R</mi><mo> </mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>And <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>k</mi><mo> </mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mtext>where </mtext><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, for reflexive <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo> </mo><mo>:</mo><mo> </mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi>R</mi><mo> </mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> which is divisible by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>So, the relation is reflexive,</p><p>Now, for symmetric <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo> </mo><mo>:</mo><mo> </mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi>R</mi><mo> </mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>k</mi><mo> </mo></math> which is divisible by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>So, the relation is symmetric,</p><p>Now for transitive relation, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo> </mo><mo>:</mo><mo> </mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi>R</mi><mo> </mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi>R</mi><mo> </mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo></math></p><p>Taking example <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>≡</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>≡</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>≡</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>But <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> which is not divisible by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>,</p><p>Hence, the relation is reflexive, symmetric but not transitive.</p>"
  }
}